nd Survivors Insurance Trust Fund\" column. I'll extract the precise values for 1947 and 1950, noting the figures are in millions of dollars. Specifically, I see the 1947 value is 1,459.5 million dollars, and I'll continue verifying the 1950 appropriation amount.\n\nI'll perform the compound annual growth rate calculation using the formula that compares the starting and ending values across the three-year period. My calculation will involve taking the nth root of the ratio between ending and starting values, where n represents the number of years growth.\n\nI calculate the ratio between 1950 and 1947 values, which yields approximately 1.4433. Then I determine the cube root of this ratio, resulting in a compound annual growth rate of about 1.1292, or 12.92% when converted to a percentage.\n\nI'll verify this calculation using a Python script to ensure precise computation, which will help me confirm the accuracy of my initial mathematical approach.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_260b35ad5f5f4728bcb05459","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"python3 << 'EOF'\nimport math\n\n# From the table - appropriations to Federal Old-Age and Survivors Insurance Trust Fund\n# FY 1947: 1,459.5 million\n# FY 1950: 2,106.4 million (Korean War started June 25, 1950, which is in FY1950)\n\nstart_value = 1459.5\nend_value = 2106.4\n\n# Number of years from FY1947 to FY1950 = 3 years\nyears = 3\n\n# CAGR = (end_value / start_value)^(1/years) - 1\ncagr = (end_value / start_value) ** (1/years) - 1\n\nprint(f\"Start value (FY1947): ${start_value} million\")\nprint(f\"End value (FY1950): ${end_value} million\")\nprint(f\"Number of years: {years}\")\nprint(f\"CAGR = ({end_value}/{start_value})^(1/{years}) - 1\")\nprint(f\"CAGR = {(end_value / start_value)**(1/years)} - 1\")\nprint(f\"CAGR = {cagr}\")\nprint(f\"CAGR as percent: {cagr * 100:.3f}%\")\nprint(f\"Rounded to nearest thousandth: {round(cagr * 100, 3)}%\")\nEOF"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
